00:41:35,380 --> 00:41:38,945
You guys know I only drag food
into this room for the Super Bowl.

771
00:41:38,960 --> 00:41:41,125
Come on, Charles. I made the pot pies.

772
00:41:41,140 --> 00:41:42,635
I should have some time with my son.

773
00:41:42,650 --> 00:41:44,060
We'll be right there.

774
00:41:46,470 --> 00:41:47,335
Your mother.

775
00:41:47,350 --> 00:41:49,155
That's a loyal woman.

776
00:41:49,170 --> 00:41:50,260
Don't.

777
00:41:50,640 --> 00:41:54,105
I'm just saying that your mother
would never let her job interf...

778
00:41:54,120 --> 00:41:56,440
She never left the kitchen, Dad.

779
00:41:56,740 --> 00:41:58,885
That's what you wanted in a wife,
not me.

780
00:41:58,900 --> 00:42:01,575
Still,
Wendy's making things difficult for you.

781
00:42:01,590 --> 00:42:02,875
Why is she still working?

782
00:42:02,890 --> 00:42:04,790
We started to discuss it.

783
00:42:05,390 --> 00:42:07,285
Legally, there's no conflict yet.

784
00:42:07,300 --> 00:42:08,670
She'll do the right thing.

785
00:42:10,190 --> 00:42:11,450
Better hope so, son.

786
00:42:14,330 --> 00:42:16,015
Danny fucking Margolis.

787
00:42:16,030 --> 00:42:17,300
What brings you back?

788
00:42:17,420 --> 00:42:18,765
When I saw you at Sun Valley,

789
00:42:18,780 --> 00:42:21,235
you said you were happy as
a clam in shit at Century.

790
00:42:21,250 --> 00:42:22,950
Well, I am.

791
00:42:23,180 --> 00:42:24,390
I was. I mean.

792
00:42:25,020 --> 00:42:26,170
You know how it is.

793
00:42:26,500 --> 00:42:27,510
Things are good there.

794
00:42:28,380 --> 00:42:30,005
I like Jerry, but I miss the family.

795
00:42:30,020 --> 00:42:32,575
Well, you had to go it on your own
with a bigger chunk of the pie.

796
00:42:32,590 --> 00:42:33,930
Yeah, true.

797
00:42:35,270 --> 00:42:37,090
Place looks great, by the way.

798
00:42:38,970 --> 00:42:40,450
Is that your rolling art out front?

799
00:42:41,270 --> 00:42:42,310
The Lambo?

800
00:42:44,600 --> 00:42:45,640
No.

801
00:42:46,420 --> 00:42:48,090
I like to sit tall in the seat.

802
00:42:48,150 --> 00:42:52,440
Look, um, I have some ideas,
and I'd love to share them with you.

803
00:42:52,990 --> 00:42:55,460
I'd love to hear them.
Come to the next dinner.

804
00:42:55,740 --> 00:42:57,405
We'll bang some steaks,
talk some concepts.

805
00:42:57,420 --> 00:42:59,395
Yeah, okay. But I was just
hoping that maybe, you know...

806
00:42:59,410 --> 00:43:00,930
No, I know what you were hoping.

807
00:43:02,600 --> 00:43:03,920
Door's always open.

808
00:43:05,850 --> 00:43:07,275
Yeah. Yeah, that's cool, Bobby.

809
00:43:07,290 --> 00:43:08,520
I-I will.

810
00:43:09,480 --> 00:43:11,030
Uh, take care.

811
00:43:48,830 --> 00:43:50,900
Hall. I need to see you.

812
00:44:05,130 --> 00:44:06,255
This is cozy.

813
00:44:06,270 --> 00:44:07,460
It's secure.

814
00:44:08,910 --> 00:44:10,885
I checked with my sources in Washington.

815
00:44:10,900 --> 00:44:14,760
There's no case file against you,
but Dan Margolis was arrested.

816
00:44:15,690 --> 00:44:17,275
He was released on his
lawyer's recognizance,

817
00:44:17,290 --> 00:44:19,700
and his arraignment's currently on hold.

818
00:44:19,730 --> 00:44:21,130
Which tells you what?

819
00:44:21,240 --> 00:44:22,750
That he's cooperating.

820
00:44:25,460 --> 00:44:26,670
Did you hear it okay?

821
00:44:26,810 --> 00:44:28,095
How the hell did you know?

822
00:44:28,110 --> 00:44:29,985
He was making too much eye contact.

823
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:31,310
Barely blinked.

824
00:44:31,450 --> 00:44:33,645
And his pulse was hammering
like he was running a marathon.

825
00:44:33,660 --> 00:44:35,420
You were smart to stay quiet.

826
00:44:35,920 --> 00:44:38,715
Look, the S.E.C. isn't the thing.

827
00:44:38,730 --> 00:44:40,205
Fines are a part of life.

828
00:44:40,220 --> 00:44:43,095
The attack you have to worry
about is the U.S. Attorney's.

829
00:44:43,110 --> 00:44:44,690
Now, here's what you're gonna do.

830
00:44:44,910 --> 00:44:47,600
One... that reporter from The Journal,

831
00:44:47,830 --> 00:44:50,770
the one that was asking about you,
he needs to be handled.

832
00:44:51,120 --> 00:44:53,455
I would do it myself,
but then he's out of the game.

833
00:44:53,470 --> 00:44:54,725
No value added.

834
00:44:54,740 --> 00:44:56,940
Better if you make him your best friend.

835
00:44:57,970 --> 00:45:02,655
And two... remember,
you don't have to outswim the shark.

836
00:45:02,670 --> 00:45:05,345
You just have to outswim the
guy you're scuba diving with.

837
00:45:05,360 --> 00:45:06,715
You want me to do that?

838
00:45:06,730 --> 00:45:08,455
You remember that night in Reykjavik?

839
00:45:08,470 --> 00:45:10,130
Wish I didn't, but I do.

840
00:45:10,470 --> 00:45:13,000
You said there was only one
thing you were afraid of.

841
00:45:14,770 --> 00:45:15,395
Windbreakers.

842
00:45:15,410 --> 00:45:17,775
Guys in windbreakers walking
in your office saying,

843
00:45:17,790 --> 00:45:19,770
"Step away from the computer."

844
00:45:19,820 --> 00:45:21,855
And you told me you'd make
sure it wouldn't happen.

845
00:45:21,870 --> 00:45:23,250
So, let me make sure.

846
00:45:25,540 --> 00:45:26,540
Look there.

847
00:45:29,880 --> 00:45:30,835
Steven Birch?

848
00:45:30,850 --> 00:45:32,230
It's either him or you.

849
00:45:34,320 --> 00:45:35,550
Memorize that?

850
00:45:38,960 --> 00:45:42,430
Well, if it's gonna be someone,
it may as well be that fraud.

851
00:45:43,270 --> 00:45:46,300
We're sharing the stage at the
Delivering Alpha Conference this week.

852
00:45:48,890 --> 00:45:52,850
He acts like he's my best friend despite
short squeezing me on HMOs last year.

853
00:45:54,080 --> 00:45:55,130
So do it.

854
00:46:00,060 --> 00:46:01,060
Hall.

855
00:46:03,440 --> 00:46:05,290
Wendy Rhoades tried to quit today.

856
00:46:07,340 --> 00:46:10,350
We've been fighting back-to-back
in the trenches for 15 years.

857
00:46:11,280 --> 00:46:12,900
But today she tried to quit.

858
00:46:13,330 --> 00:46:14,500
Still trust her?

859
00:46:16,030 --> 00:46:17,130
I want to.

860
00:46:22,820 --> 00:46:24,635
I didn't know this place
was open for lunch.

861
00:46:24,650 --> 00:46:25,760
It's not.

862
00:46:27,010 --> 00:46:29,060
- Thanks, Tony.
- My pleasure, Mr. Axelrod.

863
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:31,090
We're off the record.

864
00:46:31,630 --> 00:46:33,800
If you fuck me,
I never talk to you again.

865
00:46:33,820 --> 00:46:34,805
Got it.

866
00:46:34,820 --> 00:46:37,650
Good. If you ever want to come here,
just call me.

867
00:46:39,600 --> 00:46:42,065
Now, why was my name coming out of
your mouth at a press conference?

868
00:46:42,080 --> 00:46:44,020
Hey,
that was before you asked me to lunch.

869
00:46:46,550 --> 00:46:47,550
Jump in.

870
00:46:48,160 --> 00:46:50,025
Let's talk about those kids
you put through college.

871
00:46:50,040 --> 00:46:52,940
That's the one question gets
me walking away from the table.

872
00:46:53,710 --> 00:46:54,535
That's between them and me.

873
00:46:54,550 --> 00:46:56,550
I don't talk about it with anyone else.

874
00:47:03,920 --> 00:47:04,960
Bon appetit.

875
00:47:06,840 --> 00:47:07,775
What's next?

876
00:47:07,790 --> 00:47:10,035
Softball. Underhand.

877
00:47:10,050 --> 00:47:12,435
Give me some insight into
how you process information.

878
00:47:12,450 --> 00:47:15,290
The press acts like
information's a dirty word.

879
00:47:15,810 --> 00:47:17,445
Everyone has access to the information.

880
00:47:17,460 --> 00:47:19,400
We just know how to analyze it better.

881
00:47:20,230 --> 00:47:21,470
You answer me one.

882
00:47:22,610 --> 00:47:24,880
When did it become a crime
to succeed in this country?

883
00:47:25,240 --> 00:47:27,675
America used to salute
the guy in the limousine.

884
00:47:27,690 --> 00:47:29,185
They wanted to be the
guy in the limousine.

885
00:47:29,200 --> 00:47:30,480
They still want to.

886
00:47:30,780 --> 00:47:32,230
But now they throw eggs at it.

887
00:47:32,530 --> 00:47:34,650
I only ever went egging once.

888
00:47:35,220 --> 00:47:36,315
Biggest house in the neighborhood,

889
00:47:36,330 --> 00:47:39,660
and they never gave out any candy,
so they deserved it.

890
00:47:40,030 --> 00:47:41,475
We destroyed that place.

891
00:47:41,490 --> 00:47:43,150
Once? You're an altar boy.

892
00:47:43,470 --> 00:47:45,080
That was every Halloween for me.

893
00:47:46,100 --> 00:47:46,935
You're from around here, right?

894
00:47:46,950 --> 00:47:49,175
Yeah, Grand Concourse.
Then White Plains.

895
00:47:49,190 --> 00:47:51,895
Yeah, me too. Well, Yonkers,
but it wasn't nice back then.

896
00:47:51,910 --> 00:47:53,185
Hey, man, Yonkers used to be a place

897
00:47:53,200 --> 00:47:55,000
where you could really
get your ass kicked.

898
00:47:56,950 --> 00:47:58,800
You're a good kid for a fucking hack.

899
00:47:58,940 --> 00:48:00,840
And you're a good guy for a bankster.

900
00:48:02,430 --> 00:48:03,560
All right, fuck it.

901
00:48:03,940 --> 00:48:04,795
I wasn't gonna give you this,

902
00:48:04,810 --> 00:48:07,640
but you're here for a story
and now I like you, so...

903
00:48:09,340 --> 00:48:11,295
- Steven Birch.
- Piedmont Capital.

904
00:48:11,310 --> 00:48:12,310
Yeah.

905
00:48:12,760 --> 00:48:15,110
That swap deal he did
on Arcadian Rail Road...

906
00:48:16,240 --> 00:48:17,895
the timing is very curious.

907
00:48:17,910 --> 00:48:19,035
What kind of swap?

908
00:48:19,050 --> 00:48:20,900
I'm not gonna write the article for you.

909
00:48:22,180 --> 00:48:23,750
Do an autopsy on the deal,

910
00:48:24,620 --> 00:48:26,690
you'll find yourself a
Pulitzer in the carcass.

911
00:48:30,880 --> 00:48:32,070
Here's my cell.

912
00:48:34,270 --> 00:48:36,510
Don't call until the market closes.

913
00:48:37,390 --> 00:48:38,460
No voicemail.

914
00:48:39,810 --> 00:48:41,360
- No E-mail.
- Understood.

915
00:48:43,760 --> 00:48:44,900
Enjoy your lunch.

916
00:48:51,350 --> 00:48:53,665
How do you respond to the
criticism that hedge funds

917
00:48:53,680 --> 00:48:56,085
are the scavengers of
the financial sector

918
00:48:56,100 --> 00:48:59,735
and that a select few have
undue influence on the markets?

919
00:48:59,750 --> 00:49:03,245
Any public statement you
make or position you take

920
00:49:03,260 --> 00:49:04,965
can send a stock soaring or falling.

921
00:49:04,980 --> 00:49:06,295
We're not scavengers.

922
00:49:06,310 --> 00:49:09,825
We're white blood cells
scrubbing out bad companies,

923
00:49:09,840 --> 00:49:11,845
earning for our investors,
preventing bubbles.

924
00:49:11,860 --> 00:49:12,515
Excuse me.

925
00:49:12,530 --> 00:49:14,635
A hedge fund like mine
is a market regulator.

926
00:49:14,650 --> 00:49:17,325
I want people like Bobby
Axelrod on that wall.

927
00:49:17,340 --> 00:49:19,460
I need them on that wall.

928
00:49:19,510 --> 00:49:22,695
Axe makes my life easier by
shouting if he sees something.

929
00:49:22,710 --> 00:49:24,920
The moment I let someone
in a boardroom...

930
00:49:27,830 --> 00:49:31,510
or a government office tell
me what I can or cannot buy,

931
00:49:31,530 --> 00:49:34,800
I may as well close the shop,
and I'm not closing the shop.

932
00:49:35,060 --> 00:49:38,535
Let's touch on the role of the
activist investor in today's market.

933
00:49:38,550 --> 00:49:40,340
I'm not just playing for myself.

934
00:49:40,550 --> 00:49:44,065
I'm playing for all shareholders,
like my good friend Steven Birch here.

935
00:49:44,080 --> 00:49:47,140
Bobby Axelrod, Steven Birch,
thanks to you both.

936
00:49:59,420 --> 00:50:03,655
Um, that, uh, thing we were talking
about, they are levered four to one.

937
00:50:03,670 --> 00:50:06,800
When their accounting comes out,
it's not gonna look pretty, right?

938
00:50:07,500 --> 00:50:10,715
Those fucking guys. I wasn't told.

939
00:50:10,730 --> 00:50:12,425
I don't know why Brooks
saved those seats for them.

940
00:50:12,440 --> 00:50:14,065
I'm gonna find him and skin his ass.

941
00:50:14,080 --> 00:50:15,025
Enough.

942
00:50:15,040 --> 00:50:16,165
I'm gonna get me that scalp.

943
00:50:16,180 --> 00:50:18,375
You crushed it. Crushed.

944
00:50:18,390 --> 00:50:19,990
Let's get out of this ratfuck.

945
00:50:22,810 --> 00:50:25,265
Watch out. He may buy the building.

946
00:50:25,280 --> 00:50:27,345
It's an A-minus building.
Needs overhaul.

947
00:50:27,360 --> 00:50:29,650
He doesn't consider
anything less than triple-A.

948
00:50:29,780 --> 00:50:31,965
- Yet he hired you.
- Easy, Bryan.

949
00:50:31,980 --> 00:50:33,820
Learn anything from my talk?

950
00:50:34,440 --> 00:50:36,045
Volumes. You staying for mine?

951
00:50:36,060 --> 00:50:37,350
I know your act.

952
00:50:39,850 --> 00:50:42,370
You sending me messages?
'Cause I'm here.

953
00:50:44,400 --> 00:50:48,680
Well, the kids in my office really
thought you might buy that house.

954
00:50:49,530 --> 00:50:53,335
I told them you got big balls,
but not that big.

955
00:50:53,350 --> 00:50:55,460
Yeah, right. I'll probably pass.

956
00:50:57,150 --> 00:50:58,890
It's so nice, though, you know.

957
00:50:59,760 --> 00:51:01,850
Feels like you're part
of the beach and ocean.

958
00:51:02,170 --> 00:51:03,670
And all that air out there...

959
00:51:05,020 --> 00:51:06,450
shit, you know about it.

960
00:51:07,170 --> 00:51:09,100
Your daddy's got a
little place out there.

961
00:51:09,700 --> 00:51:12,395
He must let you use a bedroom
some weekends if you say please.

962
00:51:12,410 --> 00:51:13,740
Walk away.

963
00:51:14,860 --> 00:51:15,860
I should.

964
00:51:16,910 --> 00:51:19,480
But then again, what's the
point of having "Fuck you" money

965
00:51:20,060 --> 00:51:21,660
if you never say "Fuck you"?

966
00:51:23,950 --> 00:51:25,600
You're a smart man.

967
00:51:26,430 --> 00:51:29,060
So you know when I bring an action,

968
00:51:30,130 --> 00:51:34,490
not some county or even state,
it's the United States versus.

969
00:51:35,550 --> 00:51:36,595
Don't give me a reason.

970
00:51:36,610 --> 00:51:38,630
Oh, I know who brings an action.

971
00:51:39,970 --> 00:51:42,770
And I know what you feel about
your perfect record, too.

972
00:51:43,840 --> 00:51:46,180
You can't afford a mark
in the loss column.

973
00:51:47,350 --> 00:51:49,530
There's a saying in baseball.

974
00:51:50,180 --> 00:51:52,175
Towns fire managers.

975
00:51:52,190 --> 00:51:54,965
Owners just give them the bad news.

976
00:51:54,980 --> 00:51:58,000
You're the only one running
the big money they cheer for.

977
00:51:59,020 --> 00:52:02,055
But that's because you worked
that 9/11 shit for all it's worth.

978
00:52:02,070 --> 00:52:03,450
Fuck yourself.

979
00:52:05,050 --> 00:52:09,260
I have never sent out a single
press release, given one interview.

980
00:52:10,020 --> 00:52:12,355
I lost every one of my friends that day.

981
00:52:12,370 --> 00:52:14,860
And you've managed to
make some new ones since.

982
00:52:17,540 --> 00:52:21,365
But like I said,
they may be cheering now,

983
00:52:21,380 --> 00:52:26,090
but believe me, they are dying to boo.

984
00:52:27,580 --> 00:52:29,745
And now from the other side,

985
00:52:29,760 --> 00:52:33,530
the man whose job is to ride
herd over the bulls and bears,

986
00:52:33,550 --> 00:52:35,060
Chuck Rhoades.

987
00:52:58,130 --> 00:52:58,785
Yeah.

988
00:52:58,800 --> 00:53:03,145
Denny Dantone's coming in with an offer
on the Norton house... $62 million.

989
00:53:03,160 --> 00:53:04,935
Prepared to close in less than a week,
I hear.

990
00:53:04,950 --> 00:53:06,165
How the fuck did he see it?

991
00:53:06,180 --> 00:53:08,240
He didn't. He knew the house.

992
00:53:08,890 --> 00:53:09,980
Been to parties there.

993
00:53:10,950 --> 00:53:12,050
Son of a bitch.

994
00:53:24,890 --> 00:53:25,665
Hey, babe.

995
00:53:25,680 --> 00:53:26,680
Hey, babe.

996
00:53:27,850 --> 00:53:29,470
What the hell's wrong with Elmo?

997
00:53:30,400 --> 00:53:32,540
He went to the vet to get fixed,
remember?

998
00:53:45,080 --> 00:53:46,785
The house, I want it.

999
00:53:46,800 --> 00:53:48,975
Okay, let's take a beat.
People are gonna say that...

1000
00:53:48,990 --> 00:53:49,990
They might.

1001
00:53:50,820 --> 00:53:52,840
Offer $63 million cash.

1002
00:53:53,190 --> 00:53:54,800
Take it or leave it on the call.

1003
00:53:55,590 --> 00:53:57,000
Wire goes out first thing.

1004
00:54:16,760 --> 00:54:17,445
Yeah.

1005
00:54:17,460 --> 00:54:19,065
Mike Dimonda from The Journal.

1006
00:54:19,080 --> 00:54:20,180
Sorry to wake you.

1007
00:54:20,590 --> 00:54:21,590
I was up.

1008
00:54:22,070 --> 00:54:23,440
I'm calling for comment.

1009
00:54:23,860 --> 00:54:24,475
On?

1010
00:54:24,490 --> 00:54:28,140
Skip Wolkowska, your father's friend,
committed suicide.

1011
00:54:29,950 --> 00:54:30,970
No comment.

1012
00:55:03,320 --> 00:55:04,420
Rough morning.

1013
00:55:09,890 --> 00:55:11,880
But a reminder like this is useful.

1014
00:55:15,090 --> 00:55:17,930
What we do has consequences,

1015
00:55:18,930 --> 00:55:22,210
intended and, uh... unintended.

1016
00:55:24,440 --> 00:55:27,790
The decisions we make,
the actions we bring, have weight.

1017
00:55:31,740 --> 00:55:33,180
I'll have to carry this one.

1018
00:55:34,490 --> 00:55:35,490
So...

1019
00:55:38,340 --> 00:55:40,875
would I have given a
break to some drug dealer?

1020
00:55:40,890 --> 00:55:41,890
No.

1021
00:55:44,010 --> 00:55:47,070
So,
why would I give one to a businessman?

1022
00:55:52,760 --> 00:55:54,970
None of this should change your mission.

1023
00:55:56,780 --> 00:55:59,625
Come to work every day
